<title>ABU DHABI: Japan National Oil Corp moves Mideast office to UAE.</title>
<headline>Japan National Oil Corp moves Mideast office to UAE.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan National Oil Corp (JNOC) said it had moved its Middle East representative office to Abu Dhabi in the United Arab Emirates from Bahrain.</p>
<p>In a statement JNOC, a government body set up in 1967 to secure a stable supply of oil and natural gas to Japan, said the office would function as a liaison between its headquarters and the Middle East and parts of North Africa.</p>
<p>Between 1970 and 1976, JNOC's Middle East office was in Beirut. It then moved to London until 1981, when it moved to Bahrain. The Bahrain office was closed at the end of last month.</p>
</text>
